---
// "Bring your stack. Or borrow ours."
// Pure-prose reassurance, no links/cards/buttons. The only conversion
// moment on the page is ClosingCTA; Stack stays editorial so the bottom of
// the page doesn't read as three back-to-back CTAs (Stack → Pricing →
// ClosingCTA). Two big anchor doodles carry the section's visual weight:
// — top: hub-and-spoke (any framework, one SDK)
// — between paragraphs: a layered starter template with a "ready" badge
// Sits inside the technical+cost chapter (Scale → Stack → Pricing) and
// carries no border so the chapter stays bracketed.
---

<section id="stack" class="section">
  <div class="container-x">
    <!-- Top anchor doodle: four differently-shaped frames at the corners
         (your existing apps), dashed connectors converging on a central
         lime SDK orb. The orb has internal scribble lines so it reads as
         a chip, not just a dot. "Any framework, one connector." -->
    <div class="mx-auto mb-8 flex justify-center" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 320 120" width="280" height="105" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <!-- top-left frame: small wide -->
        <rect x="6" y="8" width="48" height="26" rx="3"/>
        <path d="M14 18 L 48 18 M 14 24 L 42 24 M 14 30 L 44 30"/>
        <!-- top-right frame: tall, denser content -->
        <rect x="266" y="6" width="46" height="36" rx="3"/>
        <path d="M274 14 L 306 14 M 274 20 L 302 20 M 274 26 L 304 26 M 274 32 L 298 32 M 274 38 L 300 38"/>
        <!-- bottom-left frame: square -->
        <rect x="14" y="76" width="42" height="32" rx="3"/>
        <path d="M22 84 L 50 84 M 22 90 L 46 90 M 22 96 L 48 96 M 22 102 L 42 102"/>
        <!-- bottom-right frame: wide -->
        <rect x="262" y="78" width="54" height="28" rx="3"/>
        <path d="M270 86 L 308 86 M 270 92 L 302 92 M 270 98 L 306 98"/>
        <!-- central SDK orb: lime fill + outline + chip-style internal lines -->
        <circle cx="160" cy="58" r="22" fill="#D7F25C"/>
        <circle cx="160" cy="58" r="22"/>
        <path d="M152 54 L 168 54 M 152 60 L 168 60 M 152 66 L 162 66" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <!-- dashed connectors, hand-drawn curves -->
        <path d="M54 22 C 90 32, 130 42, 142 50" stroke-dasharray="2 4" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        <path d="M266 24 C 230 34, 190 44, 178 50" stroke-dasharray="2 4" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        <path d="M56 92 C 90 80, 130 70, 142 64" stroke-dasharray="2 4" stroke-width="1.3"/>
        <path d="M262 92 C 230 80, 190 70, 178 64" stroke-dasharray="2 4" stroke-width="1.3"/>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="mb-8 text-center">
      <div class="eyebrow">stack</div>
      <h2 id="stack-headline" class="h-section mx-auto mt-3 max-w-[760px]">
        Bring your stack. <span class="hl">Or borrow ours.</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[640px] text-center">
      <p class="text-fg-2" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6;">
        Whatever you've built. Next.js, Remix, SvelteKit, FastAPI, Django, anything that makes HTTP calls. Midsphere fits in. The TypeScript or Python SDK is the only thing you add.
      </p>

      <!-- Mid-section anchor doodle: three layered template pages, the top
           one showing a sketched mini app layout (header bar + two
           component cards + body lines). A lime check-mark badge in the
           top-right corner signals "ready to clone, already wired." -->
      <div class="mx-auto my-12 flex justify-center" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 240 116" width="220" height="106" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <!-- back layers, slightly offset -->
          <rect x="34" y="44" width="142" height="60" rx="3"/>
          <rect x="44" y="32" width="142" height="60" rx="3"/>
          <!-- top page (raised) -->
          <rect x="54" y="20" width="142" height="60" rx="3"/>
          <!-- top page contents: header + 2 components + body lines -->
          <path d="M64 30 L 192 30"/>
          <rect x="64" y="38" width="56" height="22" rx="2"/>
          <rect x="128" y="38" width="60" height="22" rx="2"/>
          <path d="M64 68 L 184 68 M 64 73 L 174 73"/>
          <!-- lime "ready" check badge, top-right corner -->
          <circle cx="206" cy="18" r="14" fill="#D7F25C"/>
          <circle cx="206" cy="18" r="14"/>
          <path d="M199 18 L 204 23 L 214 12" stroke-width="1.6"/>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="text-fg-2" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6;">
        Starting fresh? Our starter is a working agent app, components and all. One command and you're running in a minute.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Quiet footnote, not a CTA. Stack's no-button convention stays intact:
         this reads as a margin note pointing at a deeper page, the way a
         sidebar in a printed essay points to a longer chapter. -->
    <p
      class="mx-auto mt-12 text-center font-mono"
      style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--ms-fg-3); letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
    >
      building on Next.js · Supabase · shadcn?
      <a
        href="/for-vibe-coders"
        style="color: var(--ms-fg-1); margin-left: 6px; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--ms-accent); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 4px;"
      >there's a page just for you</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
